<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kyustendil</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pautalia, Velbazhd</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kyustendil is a town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>, known for its hot springs. As Roman Pautalia it was a flourishing spa town, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, as Velbazhd, it was a regional centre near which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> in 1330. Its modern name comes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-dragas">Konstantin Dragaš</a>, whose lordship included it before the Ottoman conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kyustendil.jpg" alt="Kyustendil" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vassia Atanassova - Spiritia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kyustendil-view-and-Konyavska-mountain.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
